codex.svg uses a later commit because the Codex mark did not yet exist:

- codex.svg
  https://github.com/lobehub/lobe-icons/blob/63c800e3db6427b3f156f7b88d426ccb3f7277a1/packages/static-svg/icons/codex-color.svg

codex.svg drops the white app-icon plate and tightens its viewBox to the glyph,
so it renders at the same optical size as the other provider marks.

microsoft-color.svg is the four-square Microsoft logo, which upstream files
under the Azure name; its title is changed to "Microsoft".

lobe-icons supplies Jina as one currentColor path and no colour variant.
jina-color.svg splits that path at its two subpaths, then fills the dot with
#EB6161 and the J with #009191. These are the two dominant opaque colours in
Jina's 256x256 mark at https://jina.ai/favicon.ico.

Everything else is verbatim. Replacements come from the static-svg directory
above, since rendered-page gradient ids carry React's per-render suffix.

